    "phase": "S11_archive",
    "symptom": "panic: test_roadmap_op_self_impl FAIL [S11_archive] expected=0 got=2",
    "root_cause": "S2c (line 175) mutates the base `path` fixture via 'update --blocker self_synth.blk.1 --status_enum_adopted retired_intentional'. After S2c, the base fixture has the field set to retired_intentional, so when S11 later uses the same path as path_fail, archive PASSes instead of FAILs (the 2 failed sub-checks were 'outB contains FAIL archive' and 'outB contains blk_1_not_retired_intentional').",
    "discovery_method": "added debug println to check_s11_archive showing outB contained 'PASS archive' instead of 'FAIL archive'; inspected stale fixture dir /tmp/test_roadmap_op_self_impl.<TS>/.roadmap.self_synth which showed status_enum_adopted=retired_intentional already on blk.1 after test run",
    "fix": "added write_archive_fail_fixture() that writes a dedicated non-retired fixture (status=open, status_enum_adopted=acknowledged); replaced check_s11_archive(arch_pass_path, path) with check_s11_archive(arch_pass_path, arch_fail_path); extended track_m_chain_status signature to take arch_fail param; updated both caller sites"
  },

